---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 1,
        "name": "Home",
        "item": "https://www.alluviumbi.com/"
      },
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 2,
        "name": "Services",
        "item": "https://www.alluviumbi.com/services"
      },
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 3,
        "name": "Conversational Analytics",
        "item": "https://www.alluviumbi.com/conversational-analytics"
      }
    ]
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Ask the reports you already have | Alluvium"
  description="Ask the Power BI reports you already have, in plain questions, and get the same number the meeting already uses."
  canonicalPath="/conversational-analytics"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="service-fold">
<article>
<header class="hero"><div class="wrap">
<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><a href="/services">Services</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><span>Conversational Analytics</span></nav>
<p class="kicker">Conversational Analytics</p>
<h1>Ask the reports you already have</h1>
<p class="lede">Someone asks a question in ordinary language and gets the number from a report people already trust.</p>
<p class="hero-actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Book a Session</a></p>
</div></header>
<section class="band"><div class="wrap">
<h2>The answer has to match the meeting</h2>
<p>People already ask questions in email and in the hallway. If each answer comes from a different spreadsheet, it drifts from the figure leadership just reviewed. Revenue, margin, inventory, and cash each need one definition, and those definitions already live in your Power BI reports.</p>
<p>The question goes to those reports. The answer is the same number the report would have shown.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="band band-alt"><div class="wrap">
<h2>The question lands on the report</h2>
<p>Loose sheets stay off to the side. The question is aimed at the report the meeting already uses.</p>
<figure class="diagram"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 640 240" role="img" aria-label="A question mark points at one report. Loose sheets sit off to the side.">
<circle cx="70" cy="78" r="28" fill="none" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="6"/>
<path d="M58 70c0-12 24-14 24 2 0 10-12 10-12 20" fill="none" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
<circle cx="70" cy="112" r="4" fill="#397fb0"/>
<line x1="110" y1="96" x2="230" y2="120" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="4"/>
<rect x="236" y="36" width="150" height="176" rx="4" fill="#e7f1f8" stroke="#1c1c1c" stroke-width="2.5"/>
<rect x="256" y="58" width="110" height="16" fill="#397fb0"/>
<rect x="256" y="90" width="24" height="78" fill="#1c1c1c"/>
<rect x="292" y="114" width="24" height="54" fill="#397fb0"/>
<rect x="328" y="102" width="24" height="66" fill="#397fb0" opacity="0.75"/>
<rect x="460" y="40" width="130" height="18" rx="2" fill="#f4f4f4" stroke="#dcdcdc"/>
<rect x="478" y="70" width="130" height="18" rx="2" fill="#f4f4f4" stroke="#dcdcdc"/>
<rect x="448" y="100" width="130" height="18" rx="2" fill="#f4f4f4" stroke="#dcdcdc"/>
<rect x="492" y="130" width="120" height="18" rx="2" fill="#f4f4f4" stroke="#dcdcdc"/>
</svg><figcaption>The question points at one report. The loose sheets are not the source.</figcaption></figure>
</div></section>
<section class="band"><div class="wrap">
<h2>What has to be true first</h2>
<p>The report has to be one people already trust. There is one definition of the number, the refresh finishes in time for the meeting, and people see only the rows they should see. Someone inside the company can change a definition without a fight.</p>
<p>If that is not true yet, the questions wait. A <a href="/analytics-ai-strategy-roadmap">roadmap</a>, a <a href="/power-bi-dashboard-optimization-ai-insights">cleanup of the report you have</a>, or <a href="/power-bi-training">training on that report</a> may need to come first.</p>
<h2>Where the answer comes from</h2>
<p>You, or your analysts, ask in plain language. The answer is calculated from the Power BI reports you already run, using the same definitions the meeting already uses.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="band related-links" aria-labelledby="related-services">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="related-services">Related Power BI Services</h2>
    <ul><li><a href="/power-bi-model-health">Power BI Model Health</a></li>
<li><a href="/power-bi-dashboard-optimization-ai-insights">Dashboard Optimization</a></li>
<li><a href="/analytics-ai-strategy-roadmap">Analytics Strategy Roadmap</a></li></ul>
    <h2>Related Power BI Insights</h2>
    <ul><li><a href="/blog/conversational-analytics-needs-a-trusted-model">Conversational analytics needs a trusted model</a></li>
<li><a href="/blog/ask-the-model-dont-screenshot">Ask the model, don’t screenshot</a></li>
<li><a href="/blog/semantic-model-is-the-product">The semantic model is the product</a></li></ul>
  </div>
</section><section class="band band-cta" aria-labelledby="cta-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">Next step</p>
    <h2 id="cta-heading">Bring one report people already trust.</h2>
    <p class="lede">Book a session. We will look at that report and say whether people can ask it questions yet.</p>
    <p class="hero-actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Book a Session</a></p>
  </div>
</section></article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
